      "writtenOn": "2023-01-23T04:26:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can understand we don\u0027t need to check `mMdnsDiscoveryManager !\u003d null || mAdvertiser !\u003d null`, but why we are checking `mIsMonitoringSocketsStarted` now but we don\u0027t check it before. Is it a bug fix?",
      "revId": "eeb3fc1f99a6f3e0e20c59034ca6b33c91b263e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e025ac17_c0f41304",
        "filename": "service-t/src/com/android/server/NsdService.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 366,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T07:52:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Before, monitoring of sockets could only be started if mMdnsDiscoveryManager !\u003d null || mAdvertiser !\u003d null, because maybeStartMonitoringSockets can only be called in such cases. So maybeStopMonitoringSocketsIfNoActiveRequest can only be called in such cases. If the monitoring wasn\u0027t started, it would just possibly log some debug message. mIsMonitoringSocketsStarted \u003d\u003d true is a subset of the cases where they are non-null, and actually monitoring only needs to be stopped if it is true.\n\nAfter the change, mMdnsDiscoveryManager and mAdvertiser are always non-null, so this just uses mIsMonitoringSocketsStarted to know whether maybeStopMonitoringSocketsIfNoActiveRequest needs to be called.\n\nThat said, it\u0027s just simpler to only check mIsMonitoringSocketsStarted once inside the method, and return without logging if it\u0027s true. Updated to that.",
      "parentUuid": "3265860b_7601c555",
      "revId": "eeb3fc1f99a6f3e0e20c59034ca6b33c91b263e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c6aa6571_c5bbfe68",
        "filename": "service-t/src/com/android/server/NsdService.java",
