        "id": 1758351
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-23T04:26:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry for a newbee question, why we want to do the `mMdnsSocketClient.setCallback(mMdnsDiscoveryManager)` inside handler.post. Can\u0027t we do it directly?",
      "revId": "eeb3fc1f99a6f3e0e20c59034ca6b33c91b263e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a15ca93d_e6fcc17b",
        "filename": "service-t/src/com/android/server/NsdService.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1104,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T07:52:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "MdnsMultinetworkSocketClient is documented as non-thread-safe, meaning that it must be accessed on a consistent thread; actually setCallback has a ensureRunningOnHandlerThread check that will throw if the callback is set on a thread that is not the looper thread.\n\nFor this particular method, this is because mCallback is accessed on the looper thread and has no synchronization, so it must be written on the same thread (otherwise it could be seen as null on the looper thread for a while)",
      "parentUuid": "1e707fae_67f042f7",
      "revId": "eeb3fc1f99a6f3e0e20c59034ca6b33c91b263e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
